  "version": 9,
  "universes": 1,
  "notes": "<div><font size=\"5\"><b>Sounds in the stack</b></font></div><div>The stormy night of example 8 as a show: the stack plays the lights and the sounds together, cue by cue. Rain falls through four scenes and stops at the fifth; the music fades out while the storm goes on; the thunder and the bell play once at their cues.</div><div><b><font color=\"#ffb020\">What is in it</font></b></div><ul><li>The stage, the looks (memories 1 to 4: Night, Storm, Church, Morning), the lightning (effect 1) and the eight sounds of example 8.</li><li>A stack of 15 steps. The steps of sounds with <b>Continue</b> play on through the steps after them, with Add or without: the music (1.1), the rain (2.0), the wind (3.1) and the slow music at the end (7.1). A <b>release</b> stops each of them in its own down time: 4.0 the music, 5.1 the wind, 6.1 the rain.</li><li>The thunder (3.3), the bell (5.2) and the applause (7.0) come with <b>Add</b> and play once; the next look without Add takes them down, as it takes the lightning down. Steps 1.0, 3.0, 5.0 and 6.0 bring the looks and go on by themselves to the steps behind them.</li></ul><div><b><font color=\"#ffb020\">Try it</font></b></div><ol><li>Press <b>Stack</b> and go through the show with <b>Play</b>. The Stack view marks every step that is on in green: the steps of the sounds that play on stay green while the looks change under them.</li><li>Watch the <b>Sounds</b> view on a second device, or the row of sound faders on Main (Settings, Row of sound faders): the stack moves the faders of the sounds as it moves those of the looks.</li><li>Press <b>Stack</b> again in the middle of the storm: the sounds that play on stop, the lights stay as they are. Clear brings everything down.</li><li>On the <b>Stack</b> view, take Continue off at 2.0 (with the stack off): now the rain stops at the next look, 3.0.</li></ol>",
